#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# bar_legend

#% text
# `bar_legend(scheme)` is a colour bar legend, a value of the option `plot_legends`: in density and contour plots it colours the plot with the scheme and shows the colour bar.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# In curve plots the labels of a list argument are shown as the legend's entries. In density and contour plots the scheme is a name such as `"viridis"` (or a list of colours); `color_bar: false` hides the bar.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
plot([sin(x), cos(x)], [x, 0, 6], plot_legends: bar_legend(["a", "b"]))
#% output
#= image("bar_legend.files/bar_legend-1.svgz")

#% cell
bar_legend(["low", "high"])
#% output
#= bar_legend(["low", "high"])

#% text
# In a density plot it names the colour scheme and shows the colour bar:

#% cell
density_plot(x*y, [x, 0, 1], [y, 0, 1], plot_legends: bar_legend("viridis"))
#% output
#= image("bar_legend.files/bar_legend-3.svgz")

#% cell
density_plot(x*y, [x, 0, 1], [y, 0, 1], color_bar: true)
#% output
#= image("bar_legend.files/bar_legend-4.svgz")

#% subsection
# Possible issues

#% text
# A curve plot has no colour bar: a scheme name there is not used and the plot says so.

#% cell
plot(sin(x), [x, 0, 6], plot_legends: bar_legend("viridis"))
#% output
#| plot: options not used: plot_legends: bar_legend("viridis")
#= image("bar_legend.files/bar_legend-5.svgz")

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `color_bar`, `plot_legends`, `line_legend`, `point_legend`
